.SH NAME
goobers self-update \- stage and request a supervised binary update
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgoobers self-update\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Usage: goobers self-update [flags] [path]

Detect, stage, and smoke-check a binary target, then hand it to the stable
service supervisor. Policies are manual, on-release (default), and on-main.
Manual requires --target with a release tag; on-main fetches and builds the
configured branch at its resolved commit. This command never changes the
config repository.

Flags may also arrive as workflow inputs: policy, owner, repository, branch,
target, healthTicks, healthTimeout, and resultFile.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
goobers self-update --policy on-release
goobers self-update --policy manual --target v1.2.3
.fi
